BT /F1 13 Tf 54 597 Td (1. Define the outcome first) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 577 Td (Write the business result, budget band, timeline, and what done looks like. A vague brief) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 562 Td (invites a vague pitch. A clear brief lets you compare agencies on fit, not on slides.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 539 Td (2. Ask for proof that matches the work) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 519 Td (Review the portfolio and case studies. Look for projects like yours and results you can) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 504 Td (check. A reputable agency will show measurable outcomes, not only screenshots.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 481 Td (3. Check technical fit) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 461 Td (Confirm they build what you actually need: AI/ML, web, mobile, UX/UI, branding, animation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 446 Td (Ask who does the work. One team end to end is different from a pass-through of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 431 Td (freelancers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 408 Td (4. Watch how they communicate) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 388 Td (The first conversations are the process. Ask about project management, reporting,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 373 Td (feedback, and who owns decisions. Slow, fuzzy answers now stay slow after kickoff.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 350 Td (5. Price for value, not the lowest quote) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 330 Td (The cheapest bid often rewrites the scope later. Compare what is included, what is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 315 Td (assumed, and what support looks like after launch.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 292 Td (6. Confirm support after launch) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 272 Td (Ask who maintains the system, how issues are handled, and what the first 90 days look) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 257 Td (like. Delivery is not the finish line.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 234 Td (How AllOfTech works against this list) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 214 Td (We start with business clarity, not code. One team covers AI/ML, web, mobile, UX/UI,) Tj ET
